# Backend

The backend is an Express API hosted by `backend/Server.js`. It also serves the public `frontend/` directory and the admin dashboard.

## Local setup

From the repository root:

```powershell
npm install
$env:JWT_SECRET='local-development-secret'
$env:ADMIN_EMAIL='admin@example.com'
$env:ADMIN_PASSWORD='change-this-password'
npm start
```

The API runs at `http://localhost:4000`. The admin login is at `http://localhost:4000/admin/login.html`.

## Environment variables

- `PORT` - provided by Render; defaults to `4000`
- `JWT_SECRET` - required signing secret
- `ADMIN_EMAIL` and `ADMIN_PASSWORD` - initial admin credentials
- `ADMIN_NAME` - optional display name
- `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` - comma-separated allowed browser origins
- `DB_PATH` - optional SQLite path; Render sets it to its persistent disk

## API

- `GET /api/health`
- `POST /api/leads`
- `POST /api/auth/login`
- `POST /api/auth/logout`
- `GET /api/auth/me`
- `GET /api/leads` and `/api/leads/stats` for authenticated admins
- `GET`, `PATCH`, and `DELETE /api/leads/:id` for authenticated admins

The root `render.yaml` is the only deployment configuration. It deploys the website and backend together and creates the first admin account on startup.
